   {
    "attributes": [
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6j3d",
      "name": "Why I'm standing",
      "value": "Our country is at a crossroads. Decades ago we were atop the international income per capita table. We are now around 30th. That matters. Raising taxes will cut overall income. Becoming more productive and raising incomes across the board is the only way of countering cost of living challenges and providing the money for the quality public services we want. I'll also continue arguing for de-politicised long-term strategies to provide needed long-term direction and stability."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6j5Y",
      "name": "About me",
      "value": "I offer 35 years of service as a councillor, mayor and MP, as well as a background in finance, investment and teaching. I am privileged every day to meet with, listen to, and try to make a positive difference whether at individual, local, regional or national level. I bring an immense amount of knowledge particularly of the areas I have had responsibility for including economic development, transport, infrastructure, energy, education, local government, housing, conservation etc."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6j7T",
      "name": "Priority 1",
      "value": "Council amalgamation: ensuring authentic listening to our community before any decisions are made."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6j9O",
      "name": "Priority 2",
      "value": "Tiaki Wai: ensure far more reasonable spending & lower water charges. Current plans are unaffordable."
     },
     {
      "_key": "4mT89K6PpYj5QRKx0f6jBJ",
      "name": "Priority 3",
      "value": "Maximise economic activity/jobs inc through better use of CIT area & reviving Upper Hutt town centre."
     }
    ],
